  "body": "# AI Incident Law v0.4.4\n\n## Scope\n- Carries the source, graph, and MCP maintenance recorded in the 0.4.4 changelog, including explicit `admission_status` and `source_review_unresolved` responses, bounded MCP frame handling, and matter-monitor checkpoint recovery.\n- Updates the assistant guide to 0.1.3 with the admission-status interpretation and binds both packaged copies to the same SHA-256 manifest.\n- Retains the frozen-corpus and source-admission boundaries. No record receives a new human verification date from this package preparation.\n\n## Verification boundary\n- The source candidate is 0.4.4. The retained provider observations and hosted discovery remain evidence for published 0.4.3 until independent publication and deployment checks complete.\n- The package must pass the local build, repository checks, and packed clean-consumer smoke on the exact release candidate.\n\n## Delivery state\nThis note describes the source candidate. The v0.4.4 tag, GitHub Release, npm package, MCP Registry entry, and hosted site require separate publication and verification evidence.\n"
